        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Bumps <a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type\">file-type</a> from 21.1.1 to 21.3.0.</p>\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/releases\">file-type's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">v21.3.0</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add support for Mach-O Universal (aka \"Fat\") binaries and additional architectures (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/issues/779\">#779</a>)  d223491</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"commit-link\" href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/compare/v21.2.0...v21.3.0\">sindresorhus/file-type@<tt>v21.2.0...v21.3.0</tt></a></p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">v21.2.0</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Add support for SPSS data files (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/issues/787\">#787</a>)  889f638</li>\n<li>Add support for JMP (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/issues/784\">#784</a>)  093dba0</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"commit-link\" href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/compare/v21.1.1...v21.2.0\">sindresorhus/file-type@<tt>v21.1.1...v21.2.0</tt></a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/commit/2033ea7f1aef092e8251034b1207efc7c96ebeb0\"><code class=\"notranslate\">2033ea7</code></a> 21.3.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/commit/d223491482bda0a8222e29fe31cca7ecf65a0c4e\"><code class=\"notranslate\">d223491</code></a> Add support for Mach-O Universal (aka \"Fat\") binaries and additional architec...</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/commit/2ca86b3869a0185ec40e273ff51a9607cce2a48e\"><code class=\"notranslate\">2ca86b3</code></a> Docs: Remove BYOB stream requirement warning (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/issues/790\">#790</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/commit/4d7393ad119cdb56698a7b0575302913032c2692\"><code class=\"notranslate\">4d7393a</code></a> List <code class=\"notranslate\">@file-type/pdf</code> in available plugins (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/issues/788\">#788</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/commit/810e1d87c54beb10603855cfb654a8ce15a0cefb\"><code class=\"notranslate\">810e1d8</code></a> 21.2.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/commit/889f6384142d2b13c20898f1e1ca147b25704661\"><code class=\"notranslate\">889f638</code></a> Add support for SPSS data files (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/issues/787\">#787</a>)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/commit/093dba0055926c7e63e4dbe058e4650cde5b20d5\"><code class=\"notranslate\">093dba0</code></a> Add support for JMP (<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/issues/784\">#784</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/sindresorhus/file-type/compare/v21.1.1...v21.3.0\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores\"><img src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.\" alt=\"Dependabot compatibility score\" data-canonical-src=\"https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=file-type&amp;package-manager=npm_and_yarn&amp;previous-version=21.1.1&amp;new-version=21.3.0\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Dependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting <code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot rebase</code>.</p>\n<hr>\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br>\n<p dir=\"auto\">You can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot rebase</code> will rebase this PR</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot recreate</code> will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot merge</code> will merge this PR after your CI passes on it</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot squash and merge</code> will squash and merge this PR after your CI passes on it</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot cancel merge</code> will cancel a previously requested merge and block automerging</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot reopen</code> will reopen this PR if it is closed</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot close</code> will close this PR and stop Dependabot recreating it. You can achieve the same result by closing it manually</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot show &lt;dependency name&gt; ignore conditions</code> will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot ignore this major version</code> will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot ignore this minor version</code> will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">@dependabot ignore this dependency</code> will close this PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the PR or upgrade to it yourself)</li>\n</ul>\n</details>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42632",
            "title": "chore(deps-dev): bump file-type from 21.1.1 to 21.3.0",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-05T14:02:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-05T14:01:39.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dependabot",
                "url": "https://github.com/apps/dependabot"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/113839392?u=22cc8c5ad231d1717eceed8c957527cc1c2ce03c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This updates the Event.timeStamp documentation to remove misleading accuracy guarantees and clarify how time resolution may be affected by browser privacy settings.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #40673.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3302602284\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40673\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40673/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40673\">#40673</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42630",
            "title": "Clarify Event.timeStamp accuracy and reduced precision behavior",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-05T13:37:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-05T13:36:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "harshshah-2023",
                "url": "https://github.com/harshshah-2023"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The initial <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Scripting/What_is_JavaScript\" rel=\"nofollow\">What is JavaScript?</a> article in the Learn area has an initial example that could be improved — two of the stages of the example use screenshots, while the third uses a live example.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR changes it so that all stages use live examples, removes the unneeded screenshots, and improves the language (I've removed the reference to MDN Playground, as currently the example doesn't work in the Playground, because it doesn't respect the sandbox settings set in the live sample macro. <s>I'll submit a separate issue for that</s> — already being explored in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3613343929\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1073\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/fred/issues/1073/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/fred/issues/1073\">mdn/fred#1073</a>).</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42629",
            "title": "Improve initial what is js example",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-05T13:22:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-05T13:13:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/169272761?u=216904e59fc878dca16fb27b4b0450d5e5b69120&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a short section explaining how background-related properties<br>\nrepeat their values when fewer comma-separated values are provided than<br>\nthe number of background layers, with a concrete example.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This clarifies expected behavior when using multiple backgrounds.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42539.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3763736405\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42539\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42539/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42539\">#42539</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42627",
            "title": "Explain value repetition when fewer background values are specified",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-05T12:31:53.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-05T12:27:07.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "MUSKANNISHAD",
                "url": "https://github.com/MUSKANNISHAD"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As per <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3775854466\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42602\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42602/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42602\">#42602</a>, one of the relative URLs in the linked article appears to be incorrect. This PR aims to fix it.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42602.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3775854466\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42602\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42602/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42602\">#42602</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n",
